                <p>The importance of synthetic biology to overcome the challenges facing food security and sustainability continues to grow at an exponential rate. To identify and study genes and pathways linked to desirable traits such as root growth and density, scientists use synthetic biology tools to build highly accurate de novo assemblies, or synthetic gene circuits, containing 10 or more genes that can reach over 40kb in size. Rapid access to high-accuracy long DNA at lengths greater than 5kb can eliminate early rounds of gene synthesis and assembly, cutting out as much as 10 weeks of assembly and cloning time – a cost savings of 25% or more.</p>

